WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.320
Sloth Wants To Work!

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:39.660
I'd like... to work, please...

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.560
You came here for an interview before,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.370
and failed, remember?

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.120
I would like to live in...

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.380
I'm sorry, you fail.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:58.050
I didn't... actually come 
for an interview...

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.240
That's true.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.610
With that being said... 
could I get an interview?

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.220
Sure.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.340
Thank you...

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.840
That's great news.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.230
Yes.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.580
That would mean you're 
fired, Miss Sasako.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:15.930
What?!

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.900
I wouldn't mind having 
another part-timer.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.650
I could take more breaks that way.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.250
Then you'll become a 
sloth, Polar Bear.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.510
It'll be Sloth's Café.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.030
Sounds like a rather lazy café.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.720
Well then, let's begin the interview.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.490
Here's my résumé...

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.570
You actually made one.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.510
How long did it take you?

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.730
A month...

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.470
I think we could stop
 this interview right now.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.640
Since he worked so hard on it,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.280
please at least look at the résumé.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.570
Résumé

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.570
Name: 
Sloth

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.570
Sex

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.570
M    F

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.570
Address: 
Polar Bear's 
Café's Yard

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.070
What?!

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.650
Admitted to Mitsubayashi University
Mitsubayashi University Graduate School

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:06.650
Sloth, you went to college?!

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.020
Ph.D. Course Completed

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.610
And you even went to 
graduate school...

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.660
That's a pretty high level 
of academic achievement.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:18.590
So what was college life 
like for you, Sloth?

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.010
I was always on top of a tree...

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.050
I'm surprised you were 
able to graduate...

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:25.760
Your skills...

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.680
Skills

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.680
Research of being up in a tree

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.370
"Research of being up in a tree."

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.290
I've spent nearly all of my life...

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:35.700
living up in a tree, barely moving...

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.630
I wonder if you can 
call that a skill...

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.110
Your hobbies are...

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.530
Hobbies

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.530
Ballroom dancing

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:41.530
"Ballroom dancing."

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.530
I don't think you can 
do that up in a tree.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:49.000
Do you have any other traits 
that may be appealing?

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:55.000
I do... when I get older...

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.960
Algae grows on my body...

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.050
You pass!

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.890
What?! Why?!

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.990
Because this could be fun.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.640
You can start tomorrow.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.640
Congratulations, Mr. Sloth.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.470
I'll do my best...

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.320
I wonder if he'll be okay.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.320
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.160
Mr. Sloth hasn't shown up yet...

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.000
Maybe we should go check on him?

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.200
I'm sure he'll be here eventually.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.400
Good morning...

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.290
Hello.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.380
You actually made it. 
I'm sort of moved.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.140
How long ago did you leave your place?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.560
Twelve hours ago...

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.330
You literally spent half 
a day getting here?!

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.010
That's amazing!

00:04:56.550 --> 00:05:01.320
I'll do... my best...

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.510
Pardon me.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:04.240
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:08.240
All right, Sloth. 
Please go take her order.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.450
Okay...

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.880
How long will it take 
you to get over there?

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:22.200
About thirty minutes...

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.880
She'll probably leave.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.250
Um, I'll go take her order.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:33.050
Will you wipe off the tables, then?

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:35.130
Okay...

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.440
He's been cleaning that 
table for about two hours.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.200
He's working hard.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.570
You should learn from him, Panda.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:55.200
Watching Sloth is like being 
told that we can't hurry life.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.580
You're an absolute genius 
when it comes to

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.790
twisting thoughts to suit you.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.800
Could you wipe off 
some cups next, Sloth?

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.130
Okay...

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:16.100
So he's finally done with 
one cup after three hours.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.600
The word "eternity" comes to mind...

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.020
Eternity <i>(yukyu)</i>?

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.530
That would be a pitch <i>(toukyu)</i>.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.710
That would be table tennis <i>(takkyu)</i>.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.490
Those would be deep 
breaths <i>(shinkokyu)</i>.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.370
What does eternity mean?

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.040
It means a long time that never ends.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.030
He's asleep...

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.220
I believe he's used up his energy.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.390
I'm sorry...

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:02.130
You don't need to 
apologize, Miss Sasako.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.580
Well, he did leave his 
place before dawn,

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.650
so I guess it can't be helped.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:18.290
Sloth

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.890
His newspapers are piling up again.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:14.110
Well, he said he only 
goes home once a week.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:18.290
He should probably just 
stop getting the paper...

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.010
He apparently likes to read 
the ad inserts.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.780
By the time Sloth looks 
at the advertisements,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:30.210
I think the sales would be over.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.050
Yes, that's true...

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.510
Wow.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:47.900
Sloth

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.460
It's pretty tidy.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:44.360
Miss Sasako comes by sometimes 
to tidy up the place.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.440
Yes, I do.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.900
You're such a hard 
worker, Miss Sasako.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:49.750
Now that I think about it,

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.810
you sometimes take him shopping

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.300
and on walks, too, don't you?

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:53.860
Indeed.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.710
As 
Advertised!

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.710
All you 
can stuff!

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.710
walnuts

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:15.050
Sloth

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:09.680
Sounds like a lot of trouble.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.800
Not really.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.430
You should take me, too. 
I'll just hold on to some bamboo.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.310
You're awfully heavy, 
so I doubt that'll work.

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.550
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.260
I've always wondered something...

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:32.380
Where does your 
self-confidence come from?

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:36.110
Huh?

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.030
Sloth

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.030
My house...

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.310
Are you awake?

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:44.000
Mr. Polar Bear carried you here.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.960
So I'm fired...

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:52.990
Nope. You can come again tomorrow.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:55.660
Really?

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:59.600
Why do you want to 
work so badly, Sloth?

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:05.850
I want to treat... 
Miss Sasako to dinner...

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:07.460
Huh?

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.110
She's always helping me out...

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.560
And I can't do anything for her...

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:23.250
So I figured... I needed to be 
a hard worker at times...

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.270
Please don't worry about it.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.750
I actually want to thank you.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:31.710
What?

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:37.540
The reason I even got to 
work at Polar Bear's Café

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.930
is actually because of you, Mr. Sloth.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.390
That's true.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.920
It is because of you, Sloth.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:48.740
Mr. Polar Bear...

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.190
Not to mention,

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:55.910
I feel very relaxed when 
I'm with you, Mr. Sloth.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:10:00.200
So please, allow me to thank you.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:03.360
Miss Sasako...

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:13.160
Then I won't work... 
I'll continue being a sloth...

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:14.210
Yes.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:18.460
Then I'll continue lazing around, too.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:21.390
I think you should actually 
try working a little harder.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:27.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.090
Mr. Handa's Present.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:34.220
A Christmas present for Miss Sasako?

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.070
I know it's a little early,

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.390
but what should I get her?

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:40.950
Well...

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:44.910
Let's ask Miss Sasako what she wants.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.870
Huh? What are you 
going to ask her?

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:52.250
I'll tell her, "Mr. Handa wants 
to get you a Christmas present.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.590
What would you like?"

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:56.510
That's way too direct!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.470
Couldn't you be a little more subtle?

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.300
All right, then I'll ask,

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.330
"What gift could a person working at
 the zoo, who has feelings for you,

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:10.770
get for you without being 
too much of a burden?"

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.440
Hold on!

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.120
You're telling her everything 
with that statement, too!

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.360
What?

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:18.990
Ask her much more 
nonchalantly, please...

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:20.780
That's a rather tall order.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.070
Are you ready to order?

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:24.270
No.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.400
Mr. Handa is giving me an order.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:29.960
He's asking me to nonchalantly 
ask Miss Sasako

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.510
what she would like for Christmas.

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:34.570
Nonchalantly?

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:36.640
Rather hard, isn't it?

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:40.800
Well, is there something you'd like, Mr. Handa?

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.550
My vacuum broke, so I was thinking

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.300
I might like a new one.

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:48.500
Then let's get her a vacuum.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.270
Um, that's something that <i>I</i> want.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:52.690
Then...

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.840
How about a bench press 
set or rollers?

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:58.690
Those are things you 
want, aren't they?

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.110
Why not gather a little intel?

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.370
How?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.790
What is your favorite color?

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:11.250
A questionnaire?

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:12.640
Yep.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:14.140
For what?

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.790
It's a secret.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.460
I'll answer, too!

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:19.660
You don't have to, Panda.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:21.010
Why?

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:23.470
Because you're not Miss Sasako.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.590
What the heck?

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.090
It's important that

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:30.160
the person answering this 
questionnaire is Miss Sasako.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:31.970
It is?

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.120
Seriously, what is this?

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.760
A questionnaire only for Miss Sasako?

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:40.220
It's to find out the interests 
of young female humans.

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:41.520
I see...

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.280
Let's see...

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.540
What is your favorite color?

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.990
Black and white!

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:53.530
No, she wasn't asking you.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:54.960
Really?

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.790
Did you listen to a word we said?

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:58.910
What about you, Miss Sasako?

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:01.380
Let's see...

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.880
I don't think I really 
have a favorite color.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.400
Doesn't really have one...

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:08.050
Okay, next?

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:11.560
Um... What is your hobby?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.060
I collect panda merchandise!

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:18.880
Like I said, she's not
 asking you, Panda.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:22.330
Then what's your boring 
hobby, Mr. Penguin?

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.070
It's not boring!

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.910
More importantly, 
let's hear Miss Sasako's answer.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.810
I don't have anything that'd 
be considered a hobby...

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:33.450
Doesn't really have one... Okay, next?

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:37.420
Um, what is your latest obsession?

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.380
It would be touching pillbugs.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:43.600
What the heck?

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.300
It's an app on my phone.

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:48.880
I'm currently obsessed with a game

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.700
where you see how many of them

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:52.650
you can touch within a given time.

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:57.950
Sounds rather unusual 
for a girl your age.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:13:59.810
You think so?

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.030
You're sure a toughie, Miss Sasako.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:09.890
It's a shame that the questionnaire

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.740
we made didn't work out.

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:13.910
Indeed.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.750
Next we'll have a ladies gathering.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:17.860
Ladies gathering?

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:22.630
So, that's what's going on.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:24.340
All right.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.750
So we just have to find out 
what Miss Sasako wants

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.070
and her interests, right?

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.150
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.050
Good evening.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.560
Are you sure it's all 
right that I join you?

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.660
Of course!

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.170
Let's enjoy our chat together.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:41.980
All right.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.780
Since it's getting cold lately,

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:49.280
I've been thinking about 
buying earmuffs.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:54.870
But it's hard to find a pair 
that will fit pandas.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.120
I've been wanting gloves myself.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:02.290
But all of the ones 
on sale are too big.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.050
It's important that you keep 
warm, Mama Red Squirrel,

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.980
since you don't hibernate.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.760
How about thumb covers?

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:12.540
Sadly, those are a little tight.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.640
The thing I want right now is...

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.650
<i>We don't need to know 
what all of you want.</i>

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:22.000
<i>Please just find out what 
Miss Sasako wants!</i>

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.550
Oh, by the way, Miss Sasako.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.440
I have something I wanted to ask you.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:31.160
Yama Arashi's concert tickets 
are going on sale soon.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.740
Would you like to go 
with us, Miss Sasako?

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.650
It's so much fun!

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:40.030
I'd like to go, too!

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:43.340
But I don't know much about idols...

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:45.330
What are you talking about?

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.810
A woman must never forget 
how it feels to have a crush,

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:49.880
no matter how old she is!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.800
That's true.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.880
I'll be ordering five tickets, then.

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:55.970
Then it's settled!

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.810
It's going to be so much fun!

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.190
Which member do you like, Miss Sasako?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:03.270
Well, I don't know much about them...

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.390
Oh, really?

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:07.980
Please ask Miss Sasako 
what she wants.

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:07.980
<i>"Please ask Miss Sasako..."</i>

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.980
Then I'll tell you all about them.

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:09.770
Oh, goodness.

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:12.750
You haven't ordered 
anything yet, Miss Sasako.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:13.700
Oh my.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:15.870
I didn't even notice.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.020
Don't hold back.

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:20.060
Oh, how careless of us.

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:21.550
<i>I didn't mean her order for here...</i>

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:21.970
I know.

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:26.920
So when I was on my first date...

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:29.100
Ooh, what, what?

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.130
I couldn't believe it.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:33.250
He ordered the big parfait for us.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.960
How cute!

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:37.120
More importantly,

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.300
how'd you two end up dating?

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:42.630
Oh, that'd be too 
embarrassing to talk about.

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:45.270
We totally want to hear about 
it, don't we, Miss Sasako?

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:46.910
Yes...

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.190
On my first date...

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.660
I got you all-you-can-eat flying fish.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.970
Flying fish just isn't right!

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:58.890
I know.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:02.900
Men really don't know what 
women are thinking.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:04.020
So true.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.700
Right, Miss Sasako?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.130
Pardon me.

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:12.080
Could I get another kelp tea, please?

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.480
Oh, right away!

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:17.580
No matter how wonderful a guy may be,

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:20.490
his tail has to look amazing.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:22.540
Especially how he swings it.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:24.580
Really?

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:28.340
So the tail is what's important 
to red squirrels.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.070
It's very important.

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:33.520
Could I get another kelp tea, please?

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:34.780
Oh, right away!

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:38.850
Miss Sasako is on her fifth kelp tea.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:41.450
This plan has failed.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:44.180
Then I'll make the next move.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:06.810
<i>I wonder what Mr. Polar Bear is up to...</i>

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:10.400
<i>It appears that he's trying to be sneaky,</i>

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.020
<i>so it'd be difficult to talk to him.</i>

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:18.690
Miss Sasako was looking 
at various things,

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:20.640
but didn't buy anything.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:23.330
So I couldn't tell what she liked.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.030
I see...

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:27.990
I think we've run out of options here.

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:30.800
I wonder what I should give her...

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:32.570
Well...

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.770
Why don't you give her 
something that you

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:37.630
think would be best, Mr. Handa?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:38.960
Huh?

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:47.370
That's easier said than done...

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.620
Thank you very much.

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.290
Oh, Mr. Handa.

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:42.780
M-Miss Sasako!

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:44.940
Are you out shopping?

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:46.740
Uh, y-yes.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:49.200
Oh, perfect timing.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.170
Please take these.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:54.480
They were cheap, so I 
bought a few too many.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.130
Potatoes?

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:59.400
Oh, do you not cook?

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:02.380
These are Irish Cobbler 
potatoes, right?

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:05.820
They don't get soggy, 
so they're great for croquettes.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:09.520
Indeed. They're great for 
floured potatoes, too.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.060
Yep!

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:14.020
By the way, have you heard of 
Inka no mezame potatoes?

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:15.570
Yes.

00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:17.980
They're sweet and have a
texture like chestnuts.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.460
Those are delicious, too.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:22.340
Then there are Kitaakari potatoes...

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:24.890
Wow, you know a lot about potatoes.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.580
Well, I like them...

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:30.290
I like potatoes, too.

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:32.450
I see.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.330
Well, see you later.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.960
Oh, see you.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.440
Miss Sasako.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.140
Yes?

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.260
Please take this...

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:54.060
As sort of a thanks for the potatoes.

00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:59.020
Are you sure? 
It's wrapped up very nicely.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:02.740
Well, uh... it's for a thank you.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:06.200
Thank you very much.

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:10.030
Well, see you later.

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:11.710
See you later.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:32.980
<i>Potatoes and pebbles are alike.</i>

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:41.540
But maybe I shouldn't have given 
Miss Sasako the pebble I found...

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:45.300
It's pretty, but it's way too
early for Christmas.

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:51.900
Mr. Polar Bear.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.250
What is it, Miss Sasako?

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:56.700
I ran into Mr. Handa 
coincidentally yesterday

00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:58.720
and he gave me this...

00:21:58.720 --> 00:21:59.710
What is it?

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:03.120
It's a very cute, little 
box to put trinkets in.

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:05.670
But this was inside.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:09.140
I'm not sure what this pebble is for.

00:22:10.030 --> 00:22:11.850
It's very pretty.

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:18.310
Something good may happen

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:20.530
if you take really good care of it.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:25.000
Next Time

00:23:58.140 --> 00:23:59.660
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:01.120
What's the matter, Panda?

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:04.930
Miss Sasako always says "Enjoy" 
at the end of this, right?

00:24:04.930 --> 00:24:07.460
I wonder where she is 
when she says that?

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:08.900
You don't have to look for her.

00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:11.940
Then where does your 
trauma lie, Mr. Penguin?

00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:13.740
You don't need to look 
for that, either.

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:15.340
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:15.340 --> 00:24:17.180
Next week's Polar Bear's Café....

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:18.810
will be drawn with 
a single brush stroke!

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:20.110
What kind of announcement was that?

00:24:20.110 --> 00:24:21.090
Enjoy!

00:24:21.090 --> 00:24:23.990
Miss Sasako, where are you?

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:23.990
Grizzly's Hibernation Preparations
Grizzly's Hibernation
